  "goodToKnow": "Die Archäologie is archaeology: die Ausgrabung (excavation), der Fund (find). Famous German finds include the Nebra sky disc (Himmelsscheibe von Nebra, around 3,600 years old, the oldest known concrete depiction of the cosmos) and the Neanderthal man, named after the Neandertal valley near Düsseldorf, where bones were found in 1856. Heinrich Schliemann excavated Troy. Der Archäologe is an archaeologist. It has no plural."
